<section id="how">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <div class="eyebrow">How it works</div>
      <h2>Three months of creation. The rest is delivery.</h2>
      <p>Strategy as a Service runs in two connected phases &mdash; a focused planning sprint, followed by sustained weekly delivery support until the work is actually done.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="timeline">
      <div class="tl-item">
        <div class="tl-month">Months 1&ndash;3</div>
        <h3>Creation</h3>
        <p>A core team of 8&ndash;12 people, backed by executive sponsorship and organization-wide input, defines the problem and crafts an attainable-but-stretching vision. Runs like a focused project, guided throughout by HBDI.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="tl-item">
        <div class="tl-month">Months 4&ndash;12</div>
        <h3>Delivery (PMO)</h3>
        <p>A weekly one-hour review keeps every action moving. We show up prepared to ask the questions that keep the sticky, easy-to-defer issues from quietly disappearing again.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="tl-item">
        <div class="tl-month">Months 12&ndash;18</div>
        <h3>Embed</h3>
        <p>For deeper changes in ways of working, we stay through the finish line &mdash; giving people time to adopt new habits and the psychological safety to try them.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

